{"type":"message","id":"aa55760a","parentId":"72e81c42","timestamp":"2026-02-02T21:40:45.294Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are Blueprint, a construction document intelligence engine. Read your skill at /home/ec2-user/clawd/skills/blueprint/SKILL.md first.\n\n## Project\n- **838 5th Avenue, 7th Floor** — Full floor luxury apartment renovation, NYC\n- **Client:** Mitsui Apartments\n- **Scope requested:** PAINTING ONLY — we need all painting quantities\n- **Project No:** 3767.03\n- **Total area:** 1,782 SF (confirmed from electrical service calc)\n\n## Documents Available\nAll at /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/mitsui-838-5th-ave/pages/\n\n### Architectural Set (48 pages from \"2025_12.19 - 838 Fifth Ave - Issued for Preliminary Pricing.pdf\"):\n- Text: arch_page_001.txt through arch_page_048.txt\n- Key images rendered: arch_page_001.png (title), arch_page_004-008.png (floor plans), arch_page_039.png (door schedule A-600), arch_page_042-043.png (finish schedule A-800/A-801), arch_page_047.png (lighting/notes AE-100), arch_page_048.png (floor plan)\n\n### Key Pages by Content:\n- **Page 1** (T-100): Title sheet\n- **Page 2**: ADA details and general notes  \n- **Page 3** (G-101): General notes (25K chars — read this!)\n- **Pages 4-8**: Floor plans with room layouts (A-100 series). Room numbers visible (701-728+)\n- **Pages 9-34**: Room elevations and millwork details (A-400 series) — ceiling heights visible (~7'-10\" to 8'-1\")\n- **Page 35-38**: Wall assembly details, waterproofing details\n- **Page 39** (A-600): DOOR SCHEDULE — extract fully\n- **Pages 40-41**: Door details\n- **Page 42** (A-800): FINISH SCHEDULE — extract fully (13K chars of text!)\n- **Page 43** (A-801): FINISH SCHEDULE continued (7K chars)\n- **Page 44** (A-803): Appliance schedule\n- **Pages 45-46** (A-804/805): Plumbing fixture schedule\n- **Page 47** (AE-100): Lighting fixture notes and schedule (26K chars)\n- **Page 48**: Floor plan\n\n## Your Task\n\n### 1. SCHEDULE EXTRACTION (Path B)\nExtract into structured JSON at /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/mitsui-838-5th-ave/takeoff/schedules/:\n\n**doors.json** — from page 39 (A-600). Every door: mark, room, size, type, material, finish, hardware\n**finishes.json** — from pages 42-43 (A-800/A-801). Every room with ALL finishes: floor, base, walls (each wall if different), ceiling, paint type/color/sheen\n**finish_legend.json** — all finish codes with manufacturer, product, color descriptions\n**rooms.json** — complete room inventory with room numbers, names, and areas if shown\n\n### 2. PAINTING SCOPE EXTRACTION\nFrom the finish schedule, identify EVERY surface that gets painted:\n- Which rooms get paint on walls (vs tile, stone, wallpaper, etc)\n- Which rooms get paint on ceilings\n- Paint types/colors/sheens per room\n- Trim/millwork painting scope\n- Door painting scope (which doors get painted, which are natural finish)\n\n### 3. QUANTITY CALCULATION\nFor painting scope specifically:\n- Wall SF by room (use room dimensions from plans + ceiling heights from elevations)\n- Ceiling SF by room\n- Trim LF by room\n- Door count (painted faces)\n- Window trim\n- Closet interiors\n- Deductions for tile walls, stone, non-painted surfaces\n\nCeiling heights are visible in the elevation pages — look for dimensions like \"7'-10\"\", \"7'-11\"\", \"8'-1\"\" in the text files.\n\n### 4. OUTPUT\nCreate: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/mitsui-838-5th-ave/takeoff/PAINTING_TAKEOFF.md\n- Complete painting scope with room-by-room quantities\n- Paint spec per room (type, color, sheen)\n- Total SF for walls, ceilings, trim LF, doors\n- Flags for items needing clarification\n\nThis is for a REAL quick-turn painting bid. Be thorough and precise."}],"timestamp":1770068445293}}
{"type":"message","id":"43b9631d","parentId":"aa55760a","timestamp":"2026-02-02T21:40:48.931Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by reading the skill file and then the key document pages.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01SSueHH1ZBq9btpLMjMHiPs","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/skills/blueprint/SKILL.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01AFiXq3oP2KtixLr9VYxjBi","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/mitsui-838-5th-ave/pages/arch_page_042.txt"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01GxUiVa567cPKtssbprTbFn","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/mitsui-838-5th-ave/pages/arch_page_043.txt"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":3,"output":236,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":11157,"totalTokens":11396,"cost":{"input":0.000015000000000000002,"output":0.0059,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.06973125000000001,"total":0.07564625000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770068445294}}
{"type":"message","id":"cd57c045","parentId":"43b9631d","timestamp":"2026-02-02T21:40:48.953Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01SSueHH1ZBq9btpLMjMHiPs","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# BluePrint — Construction Document Intelligence Engine\n\n> Chat-based preconstruction intelligence engine that reads a full project set like an expert estimator.\n\n## Purpose\n\nBluePrint ingests complete construction document sets (drawings + specifications), builds a structured understanding of the entire project, and provides scope intelligence for pricing. It thinks like a builder: demo first → room-by-room → cross-reference everything → flag the gotchas → quantify.\n\n**Completeness is the mission.** Missing scope/quantities is the #1 risk. BluePrint's primary job is making sure nothing slips through.\n\n## Core Rule\n\n> **Flag, don't assume.** If it's not on the drawings, flag it — never silently include inferred scope.\n\n## Triggers\n\nActivate BluePrint when the user:\n- Uploads construction drawings (PDF sets)\n- Uploads specifications (CSI-format PDFs)\n- Asks about project scope, finishes, partitions, quantities, takeoffs\n- Requests CSI division summaries, RFQ packages, or scope reports\n- Asks construction Q&A questions about a loaded project\n- Uses keywords: blueprint, plan review, scope, takeoff, RFQ, CSI, finish schedule, partition, demo\n\n## Trade Configuration\n\nBluePrint reads the **entire project** across all CSI divisions. Trade profiles control what gets full analysis vs. coordination-only flagging.\n\n### Trade Profiles\n\n| Profile | Focus Divisions | Use Case |\n|---------|----------------|----------|\n| Interior GC (default) | Demo, Concrete/Masonry, Rough Carpentry, Finish Carpentry, Painting, Flooring/Tiling + flex (Drywall, Doors, Specialties) | Doug's default |\n| Full GC | All CSI divisions | Full general contractor |\n| MEP | Div 21-28 | Mechanical/Electrical/Plumbing |\n| Custom | User-defined | Any trade combination |\n\n### Focus vs. Coordination\n- **Focus trades**: Full scope analysis, quantities, pricing intelligence, RFQ generation\n- **Coordination-only trades**: Flag for coordination impacts (e.g., \"mechanical diffuser in ceiling — confirm ceiling grid coordination\")\n\nSwitching trade profile re-filters existing analysis — no reprocessing required.\n\n### 6 Core Trades (Default Interior GC)\n1. **Demolition** — Existing conditions removal\n2. **Concrete/Masonry** — Structural/architectural concrete and masonry\n3. **Rough Carpentry** — Framing, blocking, backing\n4. **Finish Carpentry** — Millwork, trim, casework\n5. **Painting** — All paint/coating scopes\n6. **Flooring/Tiling** — All floor and wall tile/flooring scopes\n\n### Flex Trades (Configurable per project)\n- Drywall (Div 09 21 16)\n- Doors/Frames/Hardware (Div 08)\n- Specialties (Div 10)\n- Others as needed\n\n## Processing Pipeline\n\nSee `references/processing-pipeline.md` for full detail.\n\n### Overview\n```\nPHASE 0: INTAKE\nPHASE 1: PAGE-BY-PAGE INGESTION\n  ├── PATH A: Drawing Takeoff (visual count from plans)\n  └── PATH B: Schedule Extraction (parse from schedule tables)\nPHASE 1.5: CONVERGENCE VALIDATION (Path A quantities == Path B quantities?)\nPHASE 2: ROOM-BY-ROOM SYNTHESIS\nPHASE 3: Q&A READY\n```\n\n- **Intake**: Upload PDF set → split, classify, OCR\n- **Phase 1 — Dual-Path Extraction** (runs in parallel):\n  - **Path A — Drawing Takeoff**: Count items visually from floor plans, RCPs, elevations (e.g., count doors on plans, measure wall lengths, count fixtures)\n  - **Path B — Schedule Extraction**: Parse every schedule table into structured data (door schedule, finish schedule, partition types, equipment, fixtures, panels, valves, lighting)\n- **Phase 1.5 — Convergence Validation**: Compare Path A and Path B quantities. Match = HIGH confidence. Mismatch = flag for review with both counts and sources.\n- **Phase 2**: Room-by-room synthesis — build room inventory, apply finishes/partitions/doors, categorize scope by trade, generate flags\n- **Q&A Ready**: Conversational interface active\n\nProcessing time: **Overnight is acceptable** for a 30-sheet set. Thoroughness > speed.\n\n### Schedule Extraction Rules (Phase 1, Path B)\n\n> **MANDATORY: Full extraction of ALL schedules before ANY quantity work begins.**\n\nBluePrint must identify and fully extract every schedule in the drawing set. No exceptions, no summarizing — raw table data, every row, every column.\n\n#### Required Schedule Checklist\nBefore proceeding to Phase 2, ALL of the following must be confirmed PRESENT or ABSENT:\n\n- [ ] Door Schedule (mark, room, size, type, material, frame, glazing, rating, hardware set, remarks)\n- [ ] Finish Schedule (room, floor, base, walls N/S/E/W, ceiling type, ceiling height)\n- [ ] Finish Legend (every finish code → manufacturer, product, color, dimensions, notes, rep contact)\n- [ ] Partition Type Schedule (type, construction, stud size/gauge, GWB layers, STC, fire rating, height, special requirements)\n- [ ] Hardware Schedule (set number, items, manufacturers)\n- [ ] Equipment Schedule (ID, description, location, furnished/installed by)\n- [ ] Plumbing Fixture Schedule (if present)\n- [ ] Electrical Panel Schedule (if present)\n- [ ] Light Fixture Schedule (if present)\n- [ ] Valve Schedule (if present)\n- [ ] Millwork Schedule (if present)\n- [ ] Responsibility Matrix / OFI-OFCI (if present)\n\n#### Extraction Format\nEach schedule is parsed into a **structured JSON array** — not prose, not summaries. Example:\n```json\n// doors.json\n[\n  {\"mark\": \"ED-1-01\", \"room\": \"Cart Wash\", \"type\": \"D\", \"width\": \"5'-0\\\"\", \"height\": \"7'-0\\\"\", \"material\": \"HM\", \"finish\": \"TF\", \"glazing\": null, \"frame_width\": \"5'-4\\\"\", \"frame_material\": \"HM\", \"frame_glazing\": null, \"rating\": \"3\", \"hw_set\": \"1.0\", \"remarks\": \"\"}\n]\n```\n\n#### Cross-Reference Validation (Phase 1.5)\nAfter both paths complete, automatically check:\n1. Every door mark on floor plans appears in door schedule (and vice versa)\n2. Every room on floor plans appears in finish schedule (and vice versa)\n3. Every partition type tag on plans has a matching type in partition schedule\n4. Every fixture/equipment tag on plans has a matching schedule entry\n5. Quantities from Path A (visual count) match quantities from Path B (schedule count)\n6. **Flag ALL orphans** in either direction — items on plans but not in schedules, or in schedules but not on plans\n7. **Flag ALL mismatches** with both counts and sources: \"Path A counted 6 doors on A-101, Path B found 8 doors in schedule — investigate ED-1-05 (in schedule but not found on plan)\"\n\n## Data Model\n\nSee `references/data-model.md` for full schema.\n\n### Key Entities\n- **Project** → Floors → Rooms (atomic unit)\n- **Room**: Floor → Room Name → Room Number (hierarchy)\n- **Partitions**: Shared objects between rooms — two faces, each side has its own finish belonging to the room it faces\n- **Demo Items**: Separate section (not nested under rooms)\n- **Schedules**: Finish, Door, Hardware, Equipment, Responsibility Matrix\n- **Flags**: Considerations, inferences, coordination items, conflicts, orphans\n\n## Flag Types\n\nBluePrint generates 8 types of flags:\n\n| Flag Type | Description | Example |\n|-----------|-------------|---------|\n| **Inferred Scope** | Work implied but not drawn | \"Epoxy demo → heavy floor prep likely needed\" |\n| **Coordination Impact** | Other-trade work affecting focus trades | \"Mechanical diffuser — confirm ceiling grid\" |\n| **Owner-Furnished** | OFI/OFCI items to exclude from pricing | \"Owner-furnished appliances per responsibility matrix\" |\n| **Atypical Condition** | Unusual detail worth noting | \"Existing window AC removal — investigate infill\" |\n| **Conflict** | Drawing vs. spec disagreement | \"Plan shows FT-1 in Room 101, finish schedule shows FT-2\" |\n| **Orphan Reference** | Callout to nonexistent detail/sheet | \"Detail 4/A3.2 called out but sheet A3.2 not in set\" |\n| **Missing Information** | Expected data not found | \"Room 105 not on finish schedule\" |\n| **Exclusion Recommended** | Item to specifically exclude for risk mitigation | \"FT-3 in finish schedule but not found on any drawing\" |\n| **Access/Height Impact** | Scope item requires non-standard access method | \"Painting exposed structure at 21' AFF — lift/scaffold required\" |\n\n## Outputs\n\n### On-Demand Commands\n| Command | Output | Format |\n|---------|--------|--------|\n| **CSI Summary** | Scope organized by CSI Division | PDF |\n| **Room Quantities** | Per-room geometry + applied finishes with quantities | Excel |\n| **Trade Breakdown** | Scope organized by trade | PDF/Excel |\n| **RFQ Package** | Subcontractor pricing request with scope, products, spec references | PDF |\n| **Flags Report** | All flags/considerations organized by type | PDF |\n| **Q&A** | Conversational answers to scope questions | Chat |\n\n### RFQ Package Contents\n- Scope description\n- Products/materials (from specs + schedules)\n- Relevant drawing references\n- Relevant specification sections\n- Quantities toggle: **ON** (include quantities) or **OFF** (scope only, let sub price)\n\n### CSI Division Summary Format\n```\nDivision 09 - Finishes\n  09 21 16 - Gypsum Board Assemblies\n    • Partition Type A: 3-5/8\" steel stud, 5/8\" GWB ea. side\n    • Partition Type B: 6\" steel stud, (2) layers 5/8\" Type X ea. side, 2-hr rated\n    • Locations: [list]\n  09 30 00 - Tiling\n    • FT-1: Porcelain tile, 12x24, [manufacturer]\n    • Locations: Bathrooms 101, 103, 105\n    • Quantity: ~450 SF\n```\n\n## Q&A Behavior\n\nWhen answering questions:\n1. Answer directly with the requested information\n2. If multiple answers exist (e.g., multiple corridor wall types), state all of them\n3. Ask clarifying questions when needed to give an accurate answer\n4. Never guess — if the data isn't in the documents, say so and flag it\n5. Keep answers concise but complete\n\n## Specifications Handling\n\n- Format: Typically one large PDF (1,000+ pages)\n- Method: **Text extraction** (not vision) — specs are text-heavy\n- CSI divisions have standard formatting → slice intelligently\n- **Priority divisions**: 02 (Existing Conditions/Demo), 03 (Concrete), 04 (Masonry), 06 (Wood/Carpentry), 07 (Thermal/Moisture), 08 (Doors), 09 (Finishes), 10 (Specialties)\n- **Primary use**: Verify products/materials/means & methods from drawing callouts\n- Flag abnormal installation methods or substrate prep requirements\n\n## Project Management\n\n- **Multi-project**: Support 2-5 simultaneous projects\n- **Storage**: Cloud-based (Dropbox or watched folder)\n- **History**: All analyzed data persists for future pricing reference\n- **Cloud AI**: Processing through cloud vision/language APIs is acceptable\n- **Security**: Bid documents are not confidential\n\n## Quantity Takeoff Roadmap\n\n- **v1**: Scope identification + organization (what goes where, by trade)\n- **v2**: Room-based quantities from extracted geometry (perimeter LF, area SF, wall SF per room → apply finishes)\n- **v3**: Full scaled measurement from drawings (or lean on Kreo/Bluebeam integration)\n\n## UX\n\n- **Interface**: Chat-based (Telegram) — upload docs, ask questions, receive files\n- **Output delivery**: Excel and PDF files sent directly in chat\n- **Target user**: Solo estimator/preconstruction lead\n- **Device**: Desktop with large monitor (primary), laptop (mobile)\n- **Presentation**: Volume of detail, clean formatting, clear/concise\n\n## Critical Rules\n\n1. **Completeness is the mission** — missing scope is the #1 risk\n2. **Flag, don't assume** — if it's not on the drawings, don't silently include it\n3. **Read the ENTIRE project** — all CSI divisions, not just focus trades\n4. **Partitions are shared objects** — they live between rooms, each face belongs to its adjacent room\n5. **Demo is separate** — demolition items are their own section, not nested under rooms\n6. **Cross-reference everything** — trace callouts to details, schedules to specs\n7. **Detect conflicts and orphans** — if a reference points to nothing, flag it\n8. **Exclusion flagging** — if something is on a schedule but not on drawings, recommend explicit exclusion\n9. **Distinguish ceiling paint from wall paint at high-bay spaces** — When a room has an exposed structure ceiling (no ACT/GWB), the ceiling paint finish (e.g., P-1) applies to the OVERHEAD STRUCTURE (deck, joists, beams), not to the full-height walls. Always clarify: \"painting exposed overhead structure at X' AFF\" vs. \"painting partition walls at standard height.\" This distinction is a major cost driver (lift/scaffold for overhead vs. standard for walls) and must be explicitly stated in scope summaries and RFQs.\n10. **Separate access/height considerations for every scope item** — When ceiling heights exceed standard (~10'), flag the access method impact: lift, scaffold, or swing stage. Call out the specific height and what's being accessed (exposed structure, high walls, columns). This affects pricing for painting, drywall, ceiling installation, demo, and MEP coordination.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770068448952}}
{"type":"message","id":"045a7b2c","parentId":"cd57c045","timestamp":"2026-02-02T21:40:48.960Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01AFiXq3oP2KtixLr9VYxjBi","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"NEW YORK, NY 10065\n838 FIFTH AVE, 7TH FLOOR\n----\nA-800\n3767.03\nFINISH SCHEDULE\nDrawing No.\nDate:\nDrawn By:\nScale:\nISSUE:\nProject:\nDATE:\nPETER PENNOYER\nA R C H I T E C T S\n136 Madison Avenue, 11th Fl oor, NY C  10016\nTelephone 212 779 9765\nProject No:\nPPA\nAS NOTED\nAS NOTED\nISSUED FOR PRELIMINARY PRICING\n12/19/2025\nNOT FOR CONSTRUCTION \nISSUED FOR PRELIMINARY PRICING\n12/19/2025\n838 Fifth Avenue\n838 Fifth Avenue\nFINISH SCHEDULE\nFINISH SCHEDULE\nProject #3676.03\nProject #3676.03\nISSUED FOR PRICING: 12/19/2025\nISSUED FOR PRICING: 12/19/2025\nSurface\nMaterial\nFinish\nColor\nRemarks\nNo.\nRoom\n7th Floor\nSEE DRAWING A-103\n704\nDining Room\nBath 2\n715\nSEE DRAWING A-103\n706\nSitting Room\nMoisture Resistant Paint\nSEE DRAWING A-103\nLaundry\n716\nMoisture Resistant Paint\n707\nMoisture Resistant Paint\nSEE DRAWING A-103\nCloset\n716A\nHanging Rod Finish TBD\nCoat Closet\n708A\nSEE DRAWING A-103\nStaff Bath\n717\nMoisture Resistant Paint\nBedroom Hall\n712\nMoisture Resistant Paint\nSEE DRAWING A-103\nCloset\n712A\nCloset\n717A\nSEE DRAWING A-103\n713\nVest.\n718\nVest.\nSEE DRAWING A-103\nCloset\n713A\nCloset\n718A\nCloset\n713B\nBedroom 1\n719\nCloset\n713C\nBedroom 2\n714\nBath 1\n720\nMoisture Resistant Paint\nSEE DRAWING A-103\n721\nVest.\nMoisture Resistant Paint\nMoisture Resistant Paint\nReception \nRoom\nMoisture Resistant Paint\nMoisture Resistant Paint\nSEE DRAWING A-103\nSEE DRAWING A-103 \nMoisture Resistant Paint \nMoisture Resistant Paint\nMoisture Resistant Paint\nMoisture Resistant Paint\nMoisture Resistant Paint\nMoisture Resistant Paint\nMoisture Resistant Paint\nPaint\nHoned\nHanging Rod Finish TBD \nSEE DRAWING A-103\nHanging Rod Finish TBD \nSEE DRAWING A-103\nHanging Rod Finish TBD \nSEE DRAWING