 6'-11½\" (721) | 2 faces | 28 SF | **56 SF** |\n| 1 | Double swing 4'-6\" × 6'-11½\" (726) | 2 faces | 31 SF | **62 SF** |\n| 1 | Double swing 4'-8\" × 6'-11½\" (728) | 2 faces | 32 SF | **64 SF** |\n| 3 | Existing pocket doors (704, 706, 706A) | VERIFY if painting | ~25 SF ea | **150 SF** ⚠️ |\n| **30 total** | | | | **1,270 SF** |\n\n**Door Edges:** 30 doors × ~20 LF edge = **600 LF**\n\n> ⚠️ **FLAG:** Existing pocket doors (704, 706, 706A) — Confirm if these get painted. Currently existing to remain.\n> ⚠️ **FLAG:** 7 cased openings — wood trim to be painted. Counted in casing LF per room.\n\n---\n\n## 4. QUANTITY TOTALS\n\n### Wall Paint\n\n| Category | SF |\n|---|---|\n| Standard Paint Walls | 5,163 SF |\n| Moisture Resistant Paint Walls | 867 SF |\n| **Total Wall Paint** | **6,030 SF** |\n\n### Ceiling Paint\n\n| Category | SF |\n|---|---|\n| Standard Paint Ceilings | 2,339 SF |\n| Moisture Resistant Paint Ceilings | 364 SF |\n| **Total Ceiling Paint** | **2,703 SF** |\n\n### Trim — Linear Feet\n\n| Item | LF |\n|---|---|\n| Wood Base (painted) | 847 LF |\n| Crown Molding | 397 LF |\n| Door Casing | 716 LF |\n| Window Trim (jamb/sill/head/apron) | 300 LF |\n| Panel Molding (727 only) | 41 LF |\n| **Total Trim** | **2,301 LF** |\n\n### Doors\n\n| Item | Quantity | SF |\n|---|---|---|\n| New Painted Doors (both faces) | 27 doors | 1,120 SF |\n| Existing Pocket Doors (if painted) | 3 doors | 150 SF |\n| Door Edges | 30 doors | 600 LF |\n| **Total Door Paint** | **30 doors** | **1,270 SF** |\n\n### Millwork & Specialty\n\n| Item | SF |\n|---|---|\n| Millwork Exterior (painted) | ~275 SF |\n| Vanity Exterior (painted — 715, 717, 720 only) | ~32 SF |\n| Toekick (painted) | ~38 LF |\n| Stair Risers (722, 726) | ~35 SF |\n| Closet Shelving/Millwork (painted) | ~90 SF |\n| Panelled Jambs | ~30 SF |\n| **Total Specialty Paint** | **~462 SF** |\n\n---\n\n## 5. GRAND TOTALS\n\n| Scope Item | Quantity | Unit |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Wall Paint** | **6,030** | **SF** |\n| **Ceiling Paint** | **2,703** | **SF** |\n| **Trim Paint** | **2,301** | **LF** |\n| **Door Paint** | **1,270** | **SF** |\n| **Specialty/Millwork Paint** | **462** | **SF** |\n| | | |\n| **Total Painted SF (walls + ceilings + doors + specialty)** | **~10,465** | **SF** |\n| **Total Trim LF** | **~2,301** | **LF** |\n\n---\n\n## 6. FLAGS & CLARIFICATIONS NEEDED\n\n### 🔴 Critical — Must Resolve Before Bid\n\n1. **INTERIOR DESIGNER'S PAINT SCHEDULE IS MISSING** — All paint colors, types, sheens, and number of coats are specified by the Interior Designer and NOT included in this architectural set. This is the single most important missing document for a painting bid.\n\n2. **Paint Types Unknown** — Cannot distinguish between standard latex, alkyd, specialty paints, lacquer, etc. without the ID schedule. NYC VOC regulations (Note 28 in General Notes) restrict oil-based materials — any lacquer should be sprayed off-site in a booth per the specs.\n\n3. **Number of Coats** — Not specified. Standard assumption is 2 coats over primer, but luxury residential may require 3+ coats for a hand-rubbed finish.\n\n### 🟡 Verify\n\n4. **Existing Pocket Doors (704, 706, 706A)** — Are these being painted? Schedule shows \"EXG\" with no finish specified.\n\n5. **Room 703 (Living Room) and 702 (Gallery)** — These major rooms do NOT appear in the finish schedule. Confirm if they are existing-to-remain (no painting) or if they're covered by the ID's scope.\n\n6. **Room 709 (Hall) and 708 (Powder Room Vest.)** — Not in finish schedule. Confirm scope.\n\n7. **Rooms 710 and 711 (Powder Rooms 1 & 2)** — Not in finish schedule. Confirm scope.\n\n8. **728 Primary Bath Walls** — Material is \"Plaster\" (unique in the project). Confirm if this requires special plaster primer or treatment.\n\n9. **727 Dressing Room** — Colors noted as \"Per Approved Control Sample\" rather than \"See Paint Schedule By Interior Designer.\" Confirm if this is a different paint specification.\n\n10. **Stained Millwork** — Several rooms have millwork exterior that is STAINED not painted (727 Dressing Room, 728 vanity). Confirm if staining is in painting subcontractor's scope.\n\n### 🟢 Informational\n\n11. **Lead Safe Practices Required** — General Notes #29 requires certified renovators and EPA-compliant lead-safe work practices. Pre-alteration lead testing recommended to limit regulated area.\n\n12. **VOC Restrictions** — NYC OTC guidelines in effect. Oil-based materials restricted. Lacquer must be sprayed off-site in booth. On-site spray limited to quart cans with HVLP equipment (General Notes #28).\n\n13. **Exhaust Fan Required** — Install exhaust fan (0.125% static pressure minimum) and operate until midnight on days when volatile paints/stains are applied (General Notes #24).\n\n14. **All Standard Ceiling Heights** — 7'-6\" to 8'-1\" range. No high-bay or scaffold access required.\n\n15. **Hanging Rod Finish TBD** — Multiple closets note \"Hanging Rod Finish TBD.\" Confirm if painter is responsible.\n\n---\n\n## 7. ASSUMPTIONS\n\n1. All room dimensions estimated from A-101 Construction Plan OCR dimensions + proportional scaling to 1,782 SF total. **Room dimensions should be field-verified.**\n2. Window openings assumed at 3' × 5' average for deduction purposes.\n3. Door openings deducted at 3' × 7' = 21 SF each.\n4. Stone wainscot in 728/728A assumed at 3'-6\" height.\n5. Existing-to-remain rooms (701, 702, 703, 709) excluded from scope unless directed otherwise.\n6. 2 coats paint + 1 coat primer assumed for all surfaces.\n7. Staining scope (floors, 727 millwork, 728 vanity) assumed NOT in painting subcontractor's scope.\n8. Cased openings (7 total) — wood trim is painted; counted in casing LF totals.\n\n---\n\n*Generated from architectural set: \"2025_12.19 - 838 Fifth Ave - Issued for Preliminary Pricing.pdf\" (48 pages)*  \n*Drawings referenced: A-100, A-101, A-102, A-103, A-400 through A-432, A-600, A-800, A-801*\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model